  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Private Sector Development Initiative Phase IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Private Sector Development Initiative (PSDI) is a regional technical assistance program delivered by the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and co-financed by DFAT, MFAT and the ADB. PSDI works to alleviate poverty and promote regional economic growth by supporting reforms that reduce constraints to doing business and contribute to inclusive, private sector-led economic growth. In Phase IV PSDI operates in 14 Pacific developing member countries of the ADB.</narrative>
  </description>
