   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PSDI played a pivotal role in the development and passage of Fiji&apos;s Access to Business Funding Act, which passes the Parliament in March 2025. 
&#x200d;
Since 2023, PSDI has been providing extensive support to the Fijian Ministry of Trade, Co-Operatives and SMEs and the Reserve Bank of Fiji, including technical assistance in drafting and finalising the Access to Business Finance Bill, ensuring it established a robust regulatory framework. PSDI also facilitated and led multiple stakeholder consultations, gathering feedback from various sectors to tailor the legislation to Fiji&apos;s unique financing needs. 
&#x200d;
This passing of the Act has made Fiji the first Pacific nation to introduce a comprehensive framework for innovative financing, enabling mechanisms such as crowdfunding, peer-to-peer lending, and small offer regimes. The Act aims to close the significant financing gap faced by micro, small and medium enterprises, especially those in rural areas and women-led businesses - ultimately supporting inclusive economic growth across the country.</narrative>
    </description>
